            <persName type="full">Kathleen Griffin</persName>
            <date type="birth" when="1896-11-16"/>
            <date type="death" when="1963-10-31"/>
            <note type="gender">F</note>
         </ab>
         <div type="bio">
            <p>Youngest sister of JJ’s wife <name type="person" key="barn84">Nora Barnacle</name> and closest to the Joyces. Kathleen (née Catherine) was born, like Nora, in Galway city workhouse. She attended the Convent of Mercy, and worked as a bookbinder and paper-packer. Beautiful, but with a stormy temperament, she had a disastrous affair with a married man and in 1937 (aged forty-two) married John Griffin, then a stevedore, of Middle Street, Galway. She apparently dressed as if pregnant and then (“the laughing stock of Galway”) left with her husband for London, where he followed the family trade of French-polisher. She died there in 1963. <hi rend="bold">John Simpson</hi>
                </p>
         </div>
